.Dd $Mdocdate: August 2 2026 $
.Dt Fugu::Imsg 3p
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm Fugu::Imsg
.Nd imsg messages over a connected stream socket
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal
use Fugu::Imsg;

my $imsg = Fugu::Imsg->new(fh => $socket);

$imsg->send(type => 8, data => $payload)
    or warn "send failed: $!";

my $msg = $imsg->recv(timeout => 10)
    or warn "no reply";
say $msg->{type};

$imsg->close;
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends and receives messages of the base-system
.Xr imsg_init 3
facility over a stream socket that is already connected.
.Pp
The module owns the socket:
the write loop, the
.Dv SIGPIPE
guard, the poll, and the read loop.
It owns no part of the frame.
.Vt Protocol::Imsg
frames and unframes the bytes, and this module holds one such codec.
The module never opens or names a socket, and it never logs.
Callers decide what a failure means.
.Pp
This page does not repeat the wire format:
the field layout, the length semantics, the size bounds, and the
message boundary rules.
.Vt Protocol::Imsg
documents the codec and its three limits, and the protocol reference
.Pa spec/MDNS-Imsg.md
in the OpenHAP repository gives the full specification.
That document is a curated reference, not an installed manual.
.Ss MAX_PAYLOAD
.Dv MAX_PAYLOAD
is the largest payload one message can carry, in bytes.
The module re-exports the value of the codec.
A caller that splits a long reply into messages reads it here.
.Ss new
.Fn new "fh => $fh"
creates a transport over the connected socket
.Fa $fh .
The handle is necessary.
A call without the handle is a programming error, and
.Fn new
dies.
.Ss send
.Fn send "type => $type" "data => $bytes" "peerid => $n"
frames and writes one message.
.Fa data
defaults to the empty string.
.Fa peerid
defaults to 0.
.Pp
The module treats
.Fa peerid
as opaque.
A request and response protocol puts its correlation value there and
reads it back from
.Fn recv .
The method returns 1 on success.
On failure, the method returns
.Dv undef
and sets
.Va $! .
This occurs when the connection failed earlier
.Pq Er EPIPE ,
when the payload is larger than
.Dv MAX_PAYLOAD
.Pq Er EMSGSIZE ,
or when a write error occurs.
The method tests the connection first, so a dead connection always
reports
.Er EPIPE :
the two failures have different causes, and a caller shows this
.Va $!
to the operator.
If the peer closed the socket, the method reports
.Er EPIPE .
The module suppresses
.Dv SIGPIPE
during the write.
The method refuses a payload that is too large, and it never
truncates the payload.
.Ss recv
.Fn recv "timeout => $seconds"
returns one whole message as a hash reference with
.Va type ,
.Va peerid ,
.Va pid
and
.Va data
keys.
Short reads accumulate across calls.
If several messages arrive in one read, the method returns them one
for each call.
The method returns
.Dv undef
on a timeout, on a clean end-of-file, or on an unrecoverable framing
error
.Pq Er EBADMSG .
After a framing error, the connection is dead, and every later call
returns
.Dv undef .
Without a
.Fa timeout
the call blocks until a message or an end-of-file arrives.
.Ss close
.Fn close
closes the socket and marks the connection dead.
The method is idempotent and returns 1.
A caller that owns the socket closes it here, and never by reaching
into the object.
The method also empties the decode buffer.
Thus a message that arrived before the close never comes out after
it.
.Ss is_dead
.Fn is_dead
reports if the connection can no longer carry a message.
A
.Fn close ,
an end-of-file, a write error, or a framing error all lead here.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr imsg_init 3 ,
.Xr Fugu::Mdnsd 3p
.Pp
.Vt Protocol::Imsg
documents the frame.
It is a sidecar
.Pa .pod
beside the module and not a manual page, so no cross-reference here
resolves to it.
The protocol reference
.Pa spec/MDNS-Imsg.md
in the OpenHAP repository gives the wire format.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Dick Olsson Aq Mt hi@senzilla.io
